      "message": "Not fixed, deliberately. There is no rolling upgrade to protect: the collaborative-editing API has never been released, so no deployed daemon sends the legacy \"op\"/\"aw\"/\"leave\" messages. The only peers that ever spoke them are development builds, which are rebuilt from this same series.\n\nKeeping the legacy path alive would mean two wire formats, two awareness identity models -- account URI on one side, client id on the other -- and the very defect this series fixes (two devices of one account overwriting each other\u0027s cursor) would survive in the legacy branch of the code. The commit message calls the break out explicitly.",
